{% comment %}
  OWV2 product gallery: large featured image + square thumbnail row.

  Requires: product.

  Step 1 decision (reuse vs. fallback):
  Read snippets/product-media.liquid and skimmed assets/product-thumbnails.js.
  The vendor `<product-thumbnails>` custom element binds click handlers to
  `.product__thumbnail` buttons and expects, for every thumbnail, a matching
  full media element already in the DOM at
  `[data-media-id="{{ section.id }}-{{ media.id }}"]` (built by
  `product-media.liquid`'s `.media-wrapper` / `deferred-media` markup), plus
  (for non-image media) a `#Deferred-Poster-{{ media.id }}` button to trigger
  playback, and (on desktop) an IntersectionObserver keyed to
  `[id^="Slider-Gallery"] .product__media-item` for scrollspy. That is the
  vendor's full media-slider markup, not a single "here's the current media"
  swap target — hosting it cleanly here would mean also rendering every media
  item's full deferred/model/video markup (this task ships the featured image
  only) and reproducing the vendor's section-id-prefixed data-media-id scheme.
  DECISION: do not reuse product-thumbnails.js. This snippet ships static
  markup only (featured image + `data-media-id` thumbnail buttons); the
  thumbnail-click -> main-image swap is wired with a plain click handler in
  owv2-product.js in Task 5.
{% endcomment %}
{%- if product.featured_media -%}
<div class="pdp-gallery">
  <div class="pdp-gallery__main">
    {{ product.featured_media | image_url: width: 1200 | image_tag:
       loading: 'eager', sizes: '(min-width: 750px) 55vw, 100vw',
       widths: '400,600,900,1200,1600' }}
  </div>
  {%- if product.media.size > 1 -%}
  <ul class="pdp-gallery__thumbs" role="list">
    {%- for media in product.media -%}
      <li>
        <button type="button" class="pdp-gallery__thumb" data-media-id="{{ media.id }}"
          data-full-src="{{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 1600 }}"
          aria-label="{{ 'products.product.media.load_image' | t: index: forloop.index }}">
          {{ media.preview_image | image_url: width: 200 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '100,200' }}
        </button>
      </li>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </ul>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
{%- endif -%}
